    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Khartoum was founded in 1821 as an Egyptian army outpost and became the seat of the colonial government in 1823, a trading town on the caravan route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and a focal point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>.</li><li>Mahdist forces besieged it from 13 March 1884 and took it on 26 January 1885, after which it was largely destroyed and abandoned, and Anglo-Egyptian forces refounded it as a capital after the reconquest of 1898.</li><li>It became the capital of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> in 1956, grew from 185,000 people in 1964 to an estimated 7.1 million in Greater Khartoum, and saw extensive fighting between the armed forces and the Rapid Support Forces from 2023.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>After the Mahdists took Khartoum in 1885 the survivors were deported to the newly established <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omdurman">Omdurman</a>, and when the city was rebuilt after 1898 its street plan was laid out in the shape of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-flag">Union Jack</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

